  "description": "A parametric SHOE RACK on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE TOP DECIDES WHAT IT IS. A Seat top is thicker and turns the rack into the thing you sit on to put shoes on — which is why the entrance hall wanted a bench and a rack and can have one object. A Shelf top is a plain board; Open is neither.\n\nSHELVES DIVIDE THE CLEAR HEIGHT between the base and the top, in the same bounded loop the chest and the wall cabinet use, so 1 to 8 all fill the same carcass and the published pitch tells you whether boots will fit.\n\nPAIR CAPACITY is derived — shelves × how many 240 mm pairs fit across the clear width — because \"how many shoes\" is the question a shoe rack is actually asked, and it is arithmetic nobody should do by hand.",
